---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="alert-notify Documentation: Troubleshooting"
  description="Fix common alert-notify issues: missing styles, theme mismatch, sticky toasts, wrong imports, and framework peer setups."
  pageTitle="Troubleshooting"
>
  <p>
    Common fixes when toasts look wrong, never dismiss, or fail to import in a framework project.
  </p>

  <h2>Toasts have no styles</h2>
  <p>
    The package entry injects CSS automatically for normal installs.
    If you tree-shake oddly or use a custom bundler setup, import
    <code>alert-notify/style.css</code> once near your app entry.
  </p>

  <h2>Theme does not follow my app</h2>
  <p>
    Set <code>theme: "system"</code> and ensure your document uses
    <code>html.dark</code>, <code>html.light</code>, or <code>data-theme</code>.
    Or force <code>theme: "dark"</code> / <code>"light"</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Toast never dismisses</h2>
  <p>
    Loading toasts default to <code>autoClose: false</code>.
    For sticky toasts prefer <code>autoClose: false</code> instead of <code>duration: Infinity</code>.
    Call <code>toast.dismiss(id)</code> or update the same id via promise/success.
  </p>

  <h2>Wrong import for framework helpers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>React: <code>alert-notify/react</code></li>
    <li>Vue: <code>alert-notify/vue</code></li>
    <li>Svelte: <code>alert-notify/svelte</code> (default Toaster import)</li>
    <li>Angular / Astro: core <code>alert-notify</code> only</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Svelte custom content</h2>
  <p>
    There is no Svelte <code>custom()</code> helper. Build a DOM node and pass it to
    <code>toast.custom(el)</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Still stuck?</h2>
  <p>
    Open the <a href="/examples">playground</a>, compare against
    <a href="/docs/api">API</a>, or file an issue on GitHub.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
